## Layer contract (the rule everything else rests on)

```
content/   data only — units, waves, upgrades. No logic.
sim/       deterministic game logic. No Node, no Scene, no Input, no Time,
           no unseeded RNG, no order-dependent iteration over a Dictionary.
render/    nodes, scenes, sprites, animation. Reads sim state, never writes it.
ui/        HUD and menus. Same read-only boundary to sim.
```

`sim/` classes extend `RefCounted`, never `Node`. This is what makes the replay
gate possible; a change that seems to need an exception is a design problem, not
a special case.

